{{root|en|ine-pro|*(s)ker- (cut)}}
From {{inh|en|enm|scharp}}, from {{inh|en|ang|sċearp}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*skarp}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*skarpaz}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*(s)kerb-}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*(s)ker-|t=to cut}}.

Cognate with {{cog|fy|skerp}}, {{cog|nds|scherp}}, {{m|nds|scharp}}, {{m|nds|schaarp}}, {{cog|nl|scherp}}, {{cog|de|scharf}}, {{cog|da|skarp}}. Compare {{cog|ga|cearb|t=keen; cutting}}, {{cog|la|acerbus|t=tart, bitter}}, Tocharian B {{m|xtb|kärpye|t=rough}}, Latvian {{m|lt|skârbs|t=sharp, rough}}, Russian {{m|ru|щерба|t=notch}}, Polish {{m|pl|szczerba|t=gap, dent, jag, chip, nick, notch}}, Albanian {{m|sq|harb|t=rudeness}}. More at {{l|en|shear}}.

