#: {{ux|en|The pitch pipe sounded out a perfect F♯ (F '''sharp''').}}
#: {{ux|en|Transposition frequently is harder to read because of all the '''sharps''' and flats on the staff.}}
# {{lb|en|music}} A note that is played one chromatic [[semitone]] higher than usual; denoted by the name of the note that is followed by the symbol {{angbr|{{l|mul|♯}}}}.
# {{lb|en|music}} A note that is sharp in a particular key.
#: {{ux|en|The piece was difficult to read after it had been transposed, since in the new key many notes were '''sharps'''.}}
# {{lb|en|music}} The scale having a particular sharp note as its [[tonic]].
