===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{senseid|en|Q213441}}An establishment that [[sell]]s goods or services to the public; originally only a physical location, but now a virtual establishment as well.
#* {{RQ:Cowper Task
|passage=From '''shop''' to '''shop''' <br> Wandering, and littering with unfolded silks <br> The polished counter.}}
# A place where things are [[manufacture]]d or [[craft]]ed; a [[workshop]].
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Comedy of Errors|IV|iii|passage=A tailor called me in his '''shop'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=14 Dec 86|volume=14|number=22|journal=Gay Community News|page=4|author=Willie Rice|title=He Is White And I Am Black|text=I just left Dannemora and the same thing is happening here at Auburn prison {{...}} They don't want to put me in the plate '''shop''' or let me have  a good paying job.}}
# A large [[garage]] where [[vehicle]] [[mechanic]]s work.
#: {{ux|en|The car's in the '''shop''' right now.}}
# [[workplace|Workplace]]; [[office]]. Used mainly in expressions such as ''[[shop talk]]'', ''[[closed shop]]'' and ''[[shop floor]]''.
# {{lb|en|figurative|uncountable}} Discussion of [[business]] or [[professional]] affairs.
#* {{quote-book|en|passage=What struck me about the occasion was the quiet though cheerful tone of the gathering, the restraint, noticeable also in the very few speeches. Chemistry was taboo, by common consent — no "'''shop'''" allowed.| author=South African Chemical Institute| title=Proceedings| page=28| year=1917}}
#* {{quote-book|en|passage=But Mary cut her short.<br/>"We don't allow '''shop''' at tea, Sally," she said firmly.|year=1919|author=Virginia Woolf| title=Night and Day}}
#* {{quote-book|en|passage=Nothing but '''shop''' was ever talked on any of these occasions. I am sure these close relationships were necessary for the conduct of the war, and I could not have grasped the whole position without them.| author=Winston Churchill| title=The Second World War| year=1953| chapter=Strain and Suspense| page=619}}
# A variety of classes taught in [[junior high school|junior]] or [[senior high school]] that teach [[vocation]]al skills.
# An establishment where a [[barber]] or [[beautician]] works.
#: {{co|en|a [[barber shop]]}}
# An act of shopping, especially routine shopping for food and other domestic supplies.
#: {{ux|en|This is where I do my weekly '''shop'''.}}
# {{lb|en|UK|colloquial}} The collective items bought (or to be bought) on a shopping [[trip]].
#: {{ux|en|I’ve got a big '''shop''', so feel free to go in front.}}

