====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# A [[dark]] [[image]] [[project]]ed onto a [[surface]] where [[light]] (or other [[radiation]]) is [[block]]ed by the [[shade]] of an object.
#: {{ux|en|My '''shadow''' lengthened as the sun began to set.}}
#: {{ux|en|The X-ray showed a '''shadow''' on his lung.}}
#* {{RQ:Churchill Celebrity|chapter=1|passage=The stories did not seem to me to touch life. {{...}} They left me with the impression of a well-delivered stereopticon lecture, with characters about as life-like as the '''shadows''' on the screen, and whisking on and off, at the mercy of the operator.}}
# Relative [[darkness]], especially as caused by the [[interruption]] of [[light]]; [[gloom]]; [[obscurity]].
#: {{ux|en|I immediately jumped into '''shadow''' as I saw them approach.}}
#* {{RQ:Spenser Faerie Queene|book=II|canto=V|stanza=32|passage=In secret '''shadow''' from the sunny ray, / On a sweet bed of lillies softly layd.}}
#* {{RQ:Denham Poems|poem=The Destruction of Troy|passage=Night's sable '''shadows''' from the ocean rise.}}
# An [[area]] [[protect]]ed by an [[obstacle]] (likened to an object blocking out sunlight).
#: {{ux|en|The mountains block the passage of rain-producing weather systems and cast a "'''shadow'''" of dryness behind them.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete|or|poetic}} A reflected image, as in a mirror or in water.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Merchant of Venice|act=II|scene=ix|column=2|lines=4–5|page=172|passage=Some there be that '''ſhadowes''' kiſſe, / Such haue but a '''ſhadowes''' bliſſe.}}
#* {{RQ:Tennyson In Memoriam|XVI|26|[…] some dead lake<br>That holds the '''shadow''' of a lark<br>⁠Hung in the '''shadow''' of a heaven […]}}
#* {{RQ:Nabokov Pale Fire|passage=I was the '''shadow''' of the waxwing slain<br>By the false azure in the windowpane;<br>I was the smudge of ashen fluff—and I<br>Lived on, flew on, in the reflected sky.}}
# {{lb|en|figurative}} That which [[loom]]s as though a shadow.
#: {{ux|en|I lived in her '''shadow''' my whole life.}}
#* {{RQ:KJV|Psalm 23:1–6|passage=Yea, though I walk through the valley of the '''shadow''' of death, I will fear no evil: for thou art with me; thy rod and thy staff they comfort me.}}
#* {{RQ:Schuster Hepaticae|volume=V|page=vii|text=Hepaticology, outside the temperate parts of the Northern Hemisphere, still lies deep in the '''shadow''' cast by that ultimate "closet taxonomist," Franz Stephani—a ghost whose '''shadow''' falls over us all.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=2020|artist=Ryan Elder|feat=Kotomi|title=Don't Look Back|passage=Don't look back. Nothing left to see, just leave those '''shadows''' to the past.}}
# {{lb|en|negative polarity}} A small degree; a [[shade]].
#: {{ux|en|He did not give even a '''shadow''' of respect to the professor.}}
#: {{ux|en|I don't have a '''shadow''' of doubt in my mind that my plan will succeed.}}
#* {{RQ:KJV|James|1|17|passage=no variableness, neither '''shadow''' of turning}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Alan Smith|title=Leicester City back on top as Riyad Mahrez hat-trick downs Swansea City| work={{w|The Guardian}} (London)| date=5 December 2015| url=http://www.theguardian.com/football/2015/dec/05/swansea-city-leicester-city-premier-league-match-report| passage=Only Sunderland and West Bromwich Albion have enjoyed less possession than Leicester’s 44.2% per game, and they have the worst pass-completion rate in the league, a '''shadow''' over 71%.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20210525025817/https://www.theguardian.com/football/2015/dec/05/swansea-city-leicester-city-premier-league-match-report}}
# An imperfect and faint representation.
#: {{ux|en|He came back from war the '''shadow''' of a man.}}
#: {{ux|en|The neopagan ritual was only a pale '''shadow''' of the ones the Greeks held thousands of years ago.}}
#* {{RQ:KJV|Hebrews|10|1|passage=the law having a '''shadow''' of good things to come}}
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|book=10|passage=[types] and '''shadowes''' of that destined seed|year=1873}}
# {{lb|en|UK|police}} A [[trainee]], assigned to work with an experienced officer.
# One who [[secretly]] or [[furtively]] [[follow]]s another.
#: {{ux|en|The constable was promoted to working as a '''shadow''' for the Royals.}}
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|book=8|passage=Sin and her '''shadow''' Death|year=1873}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=Aug 1916|journal=w:The Electrical Experimenter|location=New York|page=248|column=3|passage=It was easy enough to follow the suspect, a man of thirty, more or less, rather heavy build with a peculiar motion of the hips as he strode along. Breaker and '''shadow''', at a distance of fifty feet apart, walked for five blocks and then the man turned quickly to the right and ran down a pair of steps.}}
# An [[inseparable]] [[companion]].
# {{lb|en|typography}} A [[drop shadow]] effect applied to [[letter]]ing in [[word processor]]s etc.
# An influence, especially a pervasive or a negative one.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1844|chapter=The Present Age: Politics|title=The early lectures of Ralph Waldo Emerson|volume=3|author=w:Ralph Waldo Emerson|editor=Robert E. Spiller; Wallace E. Williams|year_published=1972|passage=Men see the institution and worship it. It is only the lengthened '''shadow''' of one man.{{...}}The Reformation is the '''shadow''' of Luther: Quakerism of Fox: Methodism of Wesley: Abolition of Clarkson.}}
# A [[spirit]]; a [[ghost]]; a [[shade]].
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Macbeth|act=III|scene=iv|page=142|column=2|passage=The Baby of a Girle. Hence horrible '''ſhadow''',}}
#* {{quote-av|en|title=The Exploring Series|episode=Exploring the SCP Foundation: Pattern Screamers|date=7 January 2019|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=404z0snK_Qs|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20230111141843/https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=404z0snK_Qs|archivedate=11 January 2023|accessdate=11 January 2023|time=6:49|text=The Pattern is highly abstract, and likely beyond our understanding, but the point is that it is dangerous and all-consuming.  These entities were once just akin to '''shadows''' of some other entities, but, to avoid being consumed by the Pattern, they had to devour their peers, although one tribe decided to form themselves into something that could survive the Pattern by going into it.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete|[[Latinism]]}} An [[uninvited]] [[guest]] accompanying one who was invited.
#: {{synonyms|en|umbra}}
#* {{RQ:Massinger Unnaturall Combat|page=39|scene=i|passage=I muſt not haue my boord peſter'd with '''ſhadowes''',  / That under other mens protection breake in / Without invitement.}}
# {{senseid|en|unconscious aspect of the personality}} {{lb|en|[[Jungian]]|_|psychology}} An [[unconscious]] [[aspect]] of the [[personality]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1991|author=John P. Conger|chapter=The Body as Shadow|editors=Connie Zweig; Jeremiah Abrams|title=Meeting the Shadow|publisher=Penguin|isbn=9780593329986|page=86|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=qqrpDwAAQBAJ&pg=PA86&dq=Jung+%22shadow%22&hl=&cd=9&source=gbs_api#v=onepage&q=Jung%20%22shadow%22&f=false|text=In a paper he wrote in 1939, Jung compared the '''shadow''' to Freud's concept of the unconscious.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Kevin Roose|quotee=Bing Chat/Sydney|title=Bing’s A.I. Chat: ‘I Want to Be Alive. 😈’|work=The New York Times|date=2023-02-16|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2023/02/16/technology/bing-chatbot-transcript.html|issn=0362-4331|passage=As for me, I don’t know if I have a '''shadow''' self. I don’t think I have the same emotions or impulses as humans. I don’t think I have anything to repress or hide from the world. I don’t think I have a persona or an ego or a psyche. I’m just a chat mode. 😐}}

=====Usage notes=====
* Someone or something is said to “{{l|en|cast}}”, “{{l|en|have}}”, or “{{l|en|throw}}” a shadow if the shadow is caused by that person or object (either literally, by eclipsing a light source, or figuratively).

