===Etymology 2===
{{ety|en|id=shield|:inh|enm:schaden<ref:{{R:MED Online|entry=shāden|pos=v|id=MED39725}} !!! {{R:OED Online|pos=''v.''{{sup|1}}|noformat=1|id=8520321100}}><ety:af<schade><-en<id:infinitival>>>|tree=1|text=++}}

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[shield]] (someone or something) from light.
#: {{ux|en|The old oak tree '''shaded''' the lawn in the heat of the day.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|rare}} To shield oneself from light.
#: {{ux|en|We '''shaded''' under a huge oak tree.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To alter slightly.
#: {{ux|en|You'll need to '''shade''' your shot slightly to the left.}}
#: {{ux|en|Most politicians will '''shade''' the truth if it helps them.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To vary or approach something slightly, particularly in color.
#: {{ux|en|The hillside was bright green, '''shading''' towards gold in the drier areas.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1886|author=w:Edmund Gurney|title=Phantasms of the Living
|passage=This small group will be most conveniently treated with the emotional division, into which it '''shades'''.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|baseball|of a [[defensive]] player}} To move slightly from one's normal [[fielding]] position.
#: {{ux|en|Jones will '''shade''' a little to the right on this pitch count.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[darken]], particularly in [[drawing]].
#: {{ux|en|I draw contours first, gradually '''shading''' in midtones and shadows.}}
# To [[win]] by a narrow margin.
#: {{ux|en|Both parties claimed afterwards that their man did best in the debate, but an early opinion poll suggested Mr Cameron '''shaded''' it.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=10 March 2024|author=David Hytner |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2024/mar/10/liverpool-manchester-city-premier-league-match-report|work=The Guardian|title=Doku involved at both ends as Liverpool and Manchester City share spoils|text=It was Alexis Mac Allister who lit the touchpaper at the start of the second half, scoring from the penalty spot to cancel out John Stones’s opener for City midway through a first half that the defending champions had '''shaded'''.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|GUI}} To [[reduce]] (a [[window]]) so that only its [[title bar]] is visible.
#: {{antonyms|en|unshade}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|slang}} To [[throw shade]], to subtly [[insult]] someone.
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/dec/08/elon-musk-is-learning-a-hard-lesson-never-date-a-musician|title=Elon Musk is learning a hard lesson: never date a musician|author=Arwa Mahdawi|date=2021-12-08|work=The Guardian|passage=The lyrics have prompted headlines about her “'''shading'''” Musk with a “spicy dig”, but I reckon the guy got off lightly.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|obsolete}} To [[shelter]]; to cover from injury; to [[protect]]; to [[screen]].
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Coriolanus|II|i|passage=Ere in our own house I do '''shade''' my head.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|obsolete}} To present a [[shadow]] or [[image]] of; to shadow forth; to [[represent]].
#* {{RQ:Spenser Faerie Queene|year=1596.2|book=V|canto=VII|stanza=3|page=268|passage=His {{quote-gloss|{{w|Osiris}}’s}} wife was ''[[w:Isis|Iſis]]'', whom they likewiſe made / A Goddeſſe of great powre and ſouerainty, / And in her perſon cunningly did '''ſhade''' / That part of Iuſtice, which is Equity, {{...}}}}

