{{root|en|ine-pro|*skey-}}
The verb is from {{inh|en|enm|schiften}}, from {{inh|en|ang|sċiftan|t=to divide, separate into shares; appoint, ordain; arrange, organise}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*skiftijan}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*skiftijaną}}, {{m|gem-pro|*skiptijaną}}, from earlier {{m|gem-pro|*skipatjaną|t=to organise, put in order}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*skeyb-|t=to separate, divide, part}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*skey-|t=to cut, divide, separate, part}}. Cognate with {{cog|sco|schift}}, {{m|sco|skift|t=to shift}}, {{cog|fy|skifte}}, {{m|fy|skiftsje|t=to sort}}, {{cog|nl|schiften|t=to sort, screen, winnow, part}}, {{cog|nds|schichten|t=to stack, layer}}, {{cog|de|schichten|t=to stack, layer}}, {{cog|sv|skifta|t=to shift, change, exchange, vary}}, {{cog|no|skifte|t=to shift}}, {{cog|is|skipta|t=to switch}}. See {{m|en|ship}}.

The noun is from {{inh|en|enm|schyft}}, {{m|enm|shyffte}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|schift|t=split, fissure}}, {{cog|de|Schicht|t=layer, shift}}.

