|passage=By '''shifting''' the longitude problem to the scientific community, they stifled public criticism of their inability to solve the problem. {{...}} But was it responsible governance to pass the Longitude Act without other efforts to protect British seamen? Or might it have been subterfuge—a disingenuous attempt to '''shift''' attention away from the realities of their life at sea.}}
