===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|sheltron}}, {{m|enm|sheldtrume|t=roof or wall formed by locked shields}}, from {{inh|en|ang|sċildtruma}}, {{m|ang|sċyldtruma|t=a phalanx, company (of troops), a tortoise, a covering, shed, shelter|lit=shield-troop}}, from {{m|ang|sċyld}}, {{m|ang|sċield|t=shield}} + {{m|ang|truma|t=a troop of soldiers}}. Cognate with {{cog|sco|schilthrum}}, {{m|sco|schiltrum}}. More at {{m|en|shield}}, and {{cog|ang|trymman|t=to strengthen}}, from {{m|ang|trum|t=strong, firm}} at {{l|en|trim}}.

Doublet of [[sheltron]] (a kind of military formation), which is the more conservative of the two.

