===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|countable}} Somewhere one can find [[protection]].
## A place where a person or animal may find protection from [[the elements]] (especially [[rain]], [[storm]]s, or [[cold]]) sometimes as a place to [[sleep]] (such as a cave).
##: {{ux|en|The band of explorers found a '''shelter''' behind the waterfall, which they rested at for three days.}}
##: {{ux|en|[[rock '''shelter''']]}}
## {{lb|en|usually as the head in compounds}} A [[bare-bones]] [[above-ground]] [[structure]] meant to provide [[temporary]] [[cover]] from [[the elements]]; usually small and with no door to close.
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1928|author=Lawrence R. Bourne
|title=Well Tackled!
|chapter=7|url=http://openlibrary.org/works/OL5387037W
|passage=The detective kept them in view. He made his way casually along the inside of the '''shelter''' until he reached an open scuttle close to where the two men were standing talking. Eavesdropping was not a thing Larard would have practised from choice, but there were times when, in the public interest, he had to do it, and this was one of them.}}
##: {{ux|en|[[bus '''shelter''']]}}
##: {{ux|en|[[waiting '''shelter''']]}}
## A place for protection from [[deadly]] conditions outside, including military [[assault]]; usually partly or fully underground.
##: {{ux|en|[[tornado '''shelter''']]}}
##: {{ux|en|[[fallout '''shelter''']]}}
##: {{ux|en|[[air-raid '''shelter''']]}}
## A [[refuge]], [[sanctuary]], or (''by metonymy'') [[institution]] that [[provide]]s [[temporary]] [[housing]] or a place to sleep for those [[in need]] or [[in danger]].
##: {{syn|en|home}} (''in compounds'')
##: {{ux|en|[[women's '''shelter''']]}}
##: {{ux|en|[[homeless '''shelter''']]}}
### {{lb|en|often with the definite article}} An [[animal shelter]].
###: {{ux|en|I wish more people would look for pets at the '''shelter''' before turning to breeders!}}
###: {{ux|en|[[kill '''shelter''']]}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} That which provides protection or cover.
#: {{ux|en|Along with air, water, and food, '''shelter''' is often recognized as a human necessity.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable|abstract}} The state of being protected or shielded.

====Usage notes====
The countable noun ''shelter'' has accumulated a variety of specialized meanings that all fall within the general sense of "something that provides protection". Usually, the countable use of ''shelter'' is used in implicit reference to one of the specialized senses of shelter (such as an animal shelter, homeless shelter, bomb shelter, etc.).

